 ("steps", [("Step 1 — Find the subject", "noun / pronoun that begins the sentence (often capitalised or the doer)."), ("Step 2 — Find the helping verb", "is, was, has, will, can. It usually sits right after the subject."), ("Step 3 — Find the main verb", "then locate its form (V1, V2, V3, -ing)."), ("Step 4 — Find objects and complements", "direct and indirect objects, then adverbs of manner, place and time."), ("Step 5 — Look for wh-words and linkers", "they begin clauses (when, because, so that, which)."), ("Step 6 — Build and check", "arrange in a meaningful sentence; check the grammar (tense, agreement) and punctuation.")]),
