 ("p", "You get a conversation with 4 blanks and four options for each. Choose the reply that fits the tense, the speaker's role and the sense of the next line."),
 ("h3", "Techniques"),
 ("ul", ["Read the line **before** and the line **after** the blank; the answer must connect both.", "Match the **tense**: a question 'When did you leave?' needs a past reply; 'Have you decided?' needs 'I haven't decided yet'.", "Match the **question type**: yes / no question - 'Yes, I have'; wh-question - gives the information asked.", "Check **pronouns** and **time words** for consistency (reported statements within dialogue).", "Reject options that are grammatically wrong (wrong tense, wrong word order, wrong article).", "Prefer the **polite, complete** option in formal situations (may I know ... would you mind ...)."]),
 ("h3", "Solved example"),
 ("p", "Sister: Where have you decided to stay? Brother: (a) **I haven't decided as yet.** Sister: Why are you not staying with Aunt and Uncle? Brother: (b) **They are too strict.** I won't be able to enjoy my holidays. Sister: Don't tell me you'll stay in a hotel! Brother: Definitely not (c) **I plan to stay with Rahul.** Sister: How are you both spending your vacation? Brother: (d) **We'll go sight-seeing.**"),
 ("p", "Why (a): the question uses present perfect ('have you decided'), the answer must be present perfect ('haven't decided'). Why (b): present tense general statement ('too strict') followed by the result clause. Why (c): 'Definitely not' means not a hotel; so the plan is another place. Why (d): the future ('will go') fits 'spending your vacation'."),
 ("h3", "Telephone dialogue pattern"),
 ("table", ["Function", "Model sentences"], [["Answering a call", "Yes, who is speaking, please? May I know whom you want to speak to?"], ["Asking who is calling", "Who is this? May I know who is speaking?"], ["Place of call", "Where are you calling from?"], ["Surprise / reason", "Why didn't you inform me earlier? When did you arrive?"], ["Company / accompaniment", "Are you being accompanied by someone? Are you alone?"]]),
 ("note", "IMPORTANT", "In indirect (embedded) questions the word order is statement order: *May I know **who you want** to speak to?* not *who do you want*."),
