 ("h3", "Method for completing news items"),
 ("ul", ["Identify the time: past (reported event) - simple past or present perfect; future - will + verb, is to + verb, is going to + verb.", "Identify voice: if the headline's subject is the sufferer (*Boy rescued*), use the passive; if it is the doer (*Show lands boy*), use the active.", "Expand abbreviations and numbers; add articles.", "Match the blank to the rest of the sentence: after 'when' keep the tense sequence; after 'that' use reported-speech tense."]),
 ("h3", "Solved examples"),
 ("p", "(a) CAPARO ENTERS US MARKET - The Lord Swaraj Paul Caparo group **has entered** the North American vehicle market. (b) PM TO VISIT PAKISTAN ON APRIL 11 - ... informed that Prime Minister Mr Manmohan **will be going to Pakistan on a three-day visit** in the second week of April. (c) TV SHOW LANDS BOY IN HOSPITAL - A popular show ... **has landed a 13-year-old boy in hospital**, when he filled his mouth with kerosene ... (d) KIDS FALL ILL AFTER EATING MID-DAY MEAL - 5 kids ... **fell ill** after having mid-day meal on Friday. (e) SPORTS WEEK CELEBRATION ENDS - A week-long sports day celebration ... **ended** on 22 April with a grand prize distribution ceremony."),
 ("h2", "Procedure (Process) Reporting"),
 ("p", "You are given a list of instructions (imperative) and have to complete a passage describing the process in the **passive**. The question usually gives a hint, 'Hint - is / are', for the tense."),
 ("steps", [("Step 1 — Read the instructions", "find the object of each imperative (Collect the clothes: object = the clothes)."), ("Step 2 — Convert to passive present", "object + is / are + V3 (clothes are collected)."), ("Step 3 — Join with sequence words", "first, then, after that, next, finally."), ("Step 4 — Keep numbers and plural agreement", "is for singular / uncountable, are for plural: *water is boiled; noodles are added*.")]),
 ("table", ["Imperative", "Passive"], [["Collect all the dirty white clothes.", "All the dirty white clothes are collected."], ["Soak them in a boiling water and soap solution.", "They are soaked in a mixture of boiling water and soap."], ["Take them out and beat them with fists or stick.", "They are taken out and beaten with fists or a stick."], ["Rinse them in running water until the soap is washed off.", "They are rinsed in running water until the soap content is washed off."], ["Squeeze them and hang them for drying.", "They are squeezed and hung for drying."]]),
 ("note", "REMEMBER", "Watch irregular V3: beat - beaten, take - taken, hang - hung, cut - cut, put - put, spread - spread, fry - fried, mix - mixed, grind - ground, boil - boiled."),
